  "note": "Annual election of the Aughnacloy Town Commissioners, polled Tuesday 15 January 1929. Thirteen candidates were nominated for nine seats; Frank W. Molloy, Robert Sawyer and John Brady withdrew and Samuel Henderson's nomination was invalid, leaving nine, who were declared elected (Irish News, 7 and 8 January 1929, pp. 8 and 7). Of the thirteen nominated, Molloy, Sawyer and Brady withdrew and Henderson's nomination was ruled invalid; the remaining nine are the seven old members plus Rea and Gaskin. Returned unopposed."
